fit, the input actions, the audio, and the on-screen debug overlay. Your game is
a `GameDefinition` the engine drives: the single level the game runs in, the game
mode that holds the screens and the rules, the actors and components the field is
drawn by, and the controller the ship is flown through. Register what the game
needs with the engine and use what it gives back. What remains yours is the game
itself: the field, the well, the bodies flying over it, and what its components
draw.
